<script setup lang="ts">
import BrandIcon from './BrandIcon.vue'

const shipped = [
  { name: 'Reliability', icon: 'shield', summary: 'A little less looking over your shoulder.', detail: 'Optional crash auto-restart with a crash-loop stop. Scheduled restarts warn players first, and Discord webhooks report the events nobody is watching for. Snapshot verification reads archives back and checks their coverage.' },
  { name: 'Plugin manager', icon: 'plugins', summary: 'Find the right addition. Keep it up to date.', detail: 'Search Modrinth and Hangar together, with compatibility filtering or version checks, hash-based update checks, and one-click updates that take a snapshot first. Enable and disable plugins in place. SpawnLoft manages what it installed; hand-dropped custom and premium plugins are left alone.' },
  { name: 'Server updates', icon: 'bolt', summary: 'Move forward with a way back.', detail: 'Move to the newest Paper build in one click, keeping the old jar. Crossing Minecraft versions follows a separate, confirmed, snapshot-first path because worlds can migrate one way.' },
  { name: 'Modded servers', icon: 'cube', summary: 'For worlds with their own rules.', detail: 'Fabric and NeoForge are first-class loaders with a Mods tab. Install whole modpacks from Modrinth. Pack updates may only touch files the old pack owned, preserving your other additions.' },
  { name: 'Worlds', icon: 'world', summary: 'Bring a map. Make it home.', detail: 'See every world with the active one named. Import a downloaded map from a zip or folder, export one, switch which world runs, and delete with its scope made clear. Snapshots include the active world set. A backup mirror copies every snapshot to a second location as it is taken.' },
  { name: 'Log intelligence', icon: 'terminal', summary: 'Less searching. A clearer next step.', detail: 'Recognize common failure shapes and show a suggested fix where the failure surfaces: ports already taken, EULA acceptance, wrong Java, insufficient memory or disk, missing dependencies, duplicate plugins, corrupt worlds, ticking crashes, watchdog stalls, and missing jars.' },
  { name: 'Console export', icon: 'download', summary: 'Get the right details to the right person.', detail: 'Export the console to a file, or upload it to mclo.gs after confirmation. Your account name is removed from file paths first. This was the first feature contributed from outside the project.' },
]
</script>

<template>
  <main class="roadmap-page">
    <header class="roadmap-intro roadmap-wrap"><p class="roadmap-eyebrow"><BrandIcon name="arrow" :size="16" /> THE ROAD AHEAD</p><h1>A bigger world.<br> <span>The same purpose.</span></h1><div class="intro-bottom"><p>Better tools for the server on your own PC.<br> Built around the people who make it theirs.</p><a class="roadmap-link" href="https://github.com/joogiebear/spawnloft/blob/main/ROADMAP.md">The living roadmap <BrandIcon name="external" :size="17" /></a></div></header>
    <nav class="roadmap-jumps roadmap-wrap" aria-label="Roadmap sections"><a href="#done"><span>01</span> Already here</a><a href="#after-1-0"><span>02</span> After 1.0</a><a href="#reach"><span>03</span> Further out</a><a href="#not-planned"><span>04</span> Our focus</a></nav>
    <section id="done" class="shipped-band"><div class="roadmap-wrap shipped-layout"><header class="section-intro"><p class="roadmap-eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> SHIPPED</p><h2>Good ideas.<br> Real tools.</h2><p>These capabilities are already part of SpawnLoft. Open a chapter for the details.</p><a class="roadmap-link" href="/changelog">Read the release journal <BrandIcon name="arrow" :size="17" /></a></header><div class="shipped-list"><details v-for="(item, index) in shipped" :key="item.name"><summary><span class="item-number">0{{ index + 1 }}</span><BrandIcon :name="item.icon" :size="23" /><div><h3>{{ item.name }}</h3><p>{{ item.summary }}</p></div><BrandIcon class="item-chevron" name="chevron" :size="19" /></summary><p class="shipped-detail">{{ item.detail }}</p></details></div></div></section>
    <section id="after-1-0" class="after-section roadmap-wrap"><div class="section-index"><p class="roadmap-eyebrow">02 / AFTER 1.0</p><span class="status-text">ON THE ROADMAP</span></div><div class="after-content"><p class="roadmap-eyebrow">A SHARE SCREEN</p><h2>Your people.<br> A considered way in.</h2><p class="section-lede">A clearer answer to “How do my friends join?” Sharing should be an informed choice, with the level of access made plain.</p><div class="share-options"><article><span>01 / LOCAL</span><h3>Around the house.</h3><p>Your LAN address, plainly shown for people on your home network.</p></article><article><span>02 / DIRECT</span><h3>A door you open.</h3><p>A DNS record on your own domain pointing to your home IP. UPnP would be an explicit opt-in.</p></article><article><span>03 / TUNNEL</span><h3>Another way through.</h3><p>A connection through playit.gg or a VPS relay, with no router ports opened and your home IP hidden.</p></article></div><p class="scope-note"><BrandIcon name="shield" :size="18" /><span>The planned screen would prompt you to use a whitelist and online mode when going public. It is not available yet; no release date is set.</span></p></div></section>
    <section id="reach" class="reach-section roadmap-wrap"><header><p class="roadmap-eyebrow">03 / FURTHER OUT</p><h2>More ways<br> to make it yours.</h2><p>Directions we want to explore,<br> without promising a delivery date.</p></header><div class="reach-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Easier to find. Easier to install.</h3><p>A winget manifest to bring installation to the Windows package manager. The roadmap’s proposed command is <code>winget install mcctl</code>; it is not an available installation method yet.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Beyond Windows.</h3><p>Linux and macOS are on the roadmap. Most of the engine is already portable; the Windows scheduler and platform-specific paths still need work. The desktop app is Windows-only today.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>More languages.</h3><p>Localisation is a future direction. Language support and timing have not been announced.</p></div></article></div></section>
    <section id="not-planned" class="focus-band"><div class="roadmap-wrap focus-layout"><div><p class="roadmap-eyebrow">04 / WHAT KEEPS US FOCUSED</p><h2>Built for your PC.<br> And your kind of server.</h2></div><div class="focus-copy"><p>SpawnLoft is for one person’s Windows machine: servers for friends, family, or plugin testing. The current app needs no account, cloud service, or Docker. Network access stays a deliberate decision.</p><details><summary>What isn’t on this roadmap <BrandIcon name="chevron" :size="18" /></summary><p>The desktop roadmap does not include multi-node hosting or a remotely accessible control panel. Exposing a server control panel to another machine also exposes its console. To manage SpawnLoft from elsewhere, remote into the machine that runs it.</p></details><a class="roadmap-link" href="/guide/security">Read about local control <BrandIcon name="arrow" :size="17" /></a></div></div></section>
    <footer class="roadmap-footer roadmap-wrap"><div><p class="roadmap-eyebrow">GOT SOMETHING IN MIND?</p><h2>Help shape what’s next.</h2><p>Tell us about the world you’re building and the tools you wish you had.</p></div><a class="roadmap-button" href="https://github.com/joogiebear/spawnloft/discussions/categories/ideas">Share an idea <BrandIcon name="arrow" :size="18" /></a></footer>
  </main>
